# scitex-agent-container:proxy — Apptainer recipe for kind: AgentProxy.
#
# Minimal container for the A2A *proxy* runner — forwards POST /v1/turn
# to an external AgentCard endpoint. NO claude-agent-sdk, NO node, NO
# rust, NO scitex umbrella. Just enough Python to run a Starlette app
# that re-projects an upstream AgentCard and proxies turns over HTTP.
#
# Cold-start budget: < 100 ms (the runner itself imports
# httpx + starlette + uvicorn + pyyaml — nothing else).
#
# OFF THE STAGED CHAIN, DELIBERATELY. The four-stage chain
# (01-system-deps → 02-python-pkgs → 03-base → 04-scitex) exists to share
# expensive artifacts; this recipe wants the OPPOSITE — it bootstraps straight
# from the ubuntu digest so it inherits none of that weight. Anything
# chain-shaped (``--chain``, a parent map, a bootstrap resolver) skips it by
# design; it is still ours and still built by the same CLI.
#
# Build — ALWAYS through the CLI (it stages the build context):
#   sac image build proxy -y
#   sac image build proxy --sandbox -y
#
# A RAW ``apptainer build`` OF THIS FILE IS REFUSED (PR #1018): a pre-tool-use
# hook keys on the ``org.scitex.layer`` label below and exits 2, naming the
# replacement command.
#
# Smoke test:
#   apptainer exec sac-proxy.sif python3 -c "import httpx, starlette, uvicorn, yaml; print('ok')"
#
# Why a separate SIF (vs sac-base + httpx pip-install)? Two reasons:
#   1. Trust boundary — a proxy agent is, by definition, talking to
#      something the operator doesn't fully control. Stripping the
#      runtime to the bare HTTP forwarder shrinks the attack surface
#      (no claude CLI, no SSH, no git, no shells out to arbitrary
#      tools).
#   2. Startup cost — the base image is multi-GB (rust toolchain + claude
#      SDK + node + cargo binstall'd tools, and since the four-stage split
#      the pinned heavy scientific stack as well). The proxy needs none of
#      that; a ~400 MB SIF starts noticeably faster on cold-cache
#      worker hosts.

Bootstrap: docker
# PINNED BY DIGEST — same reasoning as apptainer-01-system-deps.def: ``ubuntu:24.04``
# is a moving tag, so two builds a month apart start from different bytes.
# Kept in lockstep with the base recipe's digest (24.04.4 LTS) so the two
# top-of-stack layers share one floor.
From: ubuntu@sha256:561618e2c15bf2397621dd04f96926663a3b5616c189cf7e38db7e82f5c538ea

%files
    # Bundle the package's OWN source tree so the in-SIF sac is the
    # source tree that shipped this .def — never a `git+...@main`
    # snapshot. See apptainer-03-base.def's %files note for the staging
    # contract (cli_pkg/image_group.py sets up the build context).
    scitex-agent-container-src /opt/scitex-agent-container-src

%post
    set -e
    export DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive

    apt-get update
    apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
        ca-certificates \
        python3 python3-pip python3-venv \
        tini \
        locales tzdata
    locale-gen en_US.UTF-8
    rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

    # Bare-bones runner deps. httpx is the HTTP client (already a
    # transitive of starlette's TestClient, but we pin it explicitly so
    # the runner's `import httpx` doesn't depend on starlette internals).
    # `--break-system-packages` is needed on Ubuntu 24.04's PEP 668
    # marker — we're in a container, the "system python" IS our venv.
    python3 -m pip install --no-cache-dir --break-system-packages \
        "httpx>=0.27,<1" \
        "starlette>=0.37,<1" \
        "uvicorn>=0.30,<1" \
        "pyyaml>=6,<7"

    # Install the sac runner module itself. The proxy runner module
    # (scitex_agent_container._runners.a2a_proxy) lives in this package;
    # without it the apptainer dispatch's `python3 -m ...` invocation
    # fails with ModuleNotFoundError. The source tree is bundled via
    # the %files section above — installing from /opt/... structurally
    # pins the SIF's sac to whatever shipped the .def.
    python3 -m pip install --no-cache-dir --break-system-packages \
        /opt/scitex-agent-container-src

    # Convenience symlink — same rationale as apptainer-01-system-deps.def: many
    # tools hard-code `python` rather than `python3`.
    ln -sf /usr/bin/python3 /usr/local/bin/python

%environment
    export LANG=en_US.UTF-8
    export LC_ALL=en_US.UTF-8

%labels
    org.scitex.layer proxy
    org.scitex.runtime apptainer
    org.scitex.kind AgentProxy
    org.scitex.contains "python3 httpx starlette uvicorn pyyaml tini"

%help
    scitex-agent-container :proxy layer.
    Minimal HTTP forwarder for kind: AgentProxy agents. Forwards
    POST /v1/turn to an external A2A endpoint and re-projects the
    upstream AgentCard at /.well-known/agent-card.json with our own
    name + URL. No claude-agent-sdk, no shell tooling — defense in
    depth for the untrusted-upstream case.
